Subject: [PATCH] libnvdimm: the pmem driver needs ND_CLAIM on its own

nd_pmem_probe() enables every namespace through devm_namespace_enable()
-> devm_nsio_enable(), which lives in claim.c and is built only with
CONFIG_ND_CLAIM. That symbol is selected by BTT and NVDIMM_PFN alone, so
with both off (no ZONE_DEVICE, no BTT) the stub in nd-core.h returns
-ENXIO and even a raw namespace never gets its /dev/pmemN.

Select ND_CLAIM from BLK_DEV_PMEM.

--- a/drivers/nvdimm/Kconfig	2026-10-30 13:06:41.000000000 +0100
+++ b/drivers/nvdimm/Kconfig	2026-11-04 12:21:16.387951372 +0100
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 	tristate "PMEM: Persistent memory block device support"
 	default LIBNVDIMM
 	select DAX
+	select ND_CLAIM
 	select ND_BTT if BTT
 	select ND_PFN if NVDIMM_PFN
 	help
